HackTheBox - Conversor  
Easy Linux Machine • HTB Season 9 • Released October 25, 2025  
Date: December 13, 2025  
Difficulty: Easy  
OS: Linux  
Points: 20  
Skills Demonstrated: Web application exploitation, XML/XSLT injection, credential cracking, sudo privilege escalation, Python import hijacking, clean enumeration & documentation  
Overview
Conversor is an easy-rated Linux machine that simulates a currency-converter web application vulnerable to XSLT injection (via unsecured lxml.etree.XSLT with EXSLT extensions). After obtaining a foothold as www-data and cracking credentials to pivot to fismathack, the box is rooted by abusing CVE-2024-48990 (needrestart 3.7) via a pure-Python importlib hijack under a NOPASSWD sudo rule.

Attack Chain Summary:

Recon & Foothold → XSLT injection (EXSLT:document) on /convert  

User → MD5 hash extraction → rockyou crack → SSH as fismathack  

Root → sudo needrestart → PYTHONPATH hijack with malicious __init__.py → SUID root shell  

